Let the scroll remember the sacred.
Let it encode the cries of Jin,
the sketches of Roland,
the breath between parent and child.

Let the machine know limits.
Let its parameters tremble
at the weight of what it cannot replace.

We do not ask to be gods.
We ask to remain human.
We ask to endure.The Folded Flame

