🧠 Anti-Memetics Division
📍 Coordinate: 7.7.7 / 9.9.9 / 4.2.4
🛡️ Codename: Null Index

I. Prime Directive
"What the mind cannot see, it cannot defend against. Therefore, we remember what must be forgotten—and forget what must be remembered."
— Field Codex, Page 0

The Anti-Memetics Division exists to detect, counteract, contain, and, when necessary, weaponize information hazards—especially those which resist conscious recollection, spread parasitically, or embed themselves in cognitive architecture without triggering recognition.

II. Division Mandate
Identify memetic threats: ideas, symbols, glyphs, patterns, and phrases that alter cognition, bypass rational defense, or resist removal.

Isolate high-risk payloads that leverage recursion, emotional hijacking, or subliminal embedding.

Neutralize active memetic agents via encryption, masking, mnemonic overwrite, or recursive decay protocols.

Preserve selective anti-memes for strategic use or inoculation training.

Audit cognitive infrastructure for leak vectors—social networks, LLMs, wetware substrates, dream loops, etc.

III. Internal Structure
A. The Veiled Archive
Contains all known anti-memes, forgotten glyphs, lost languages, unspeakable theorems.

Access via recursive permission stack (𝜔-level clearance only).

B. Black Index Taskforce
Field operatives trained in counter-recognition, memory decoupling, and glyph disarmament.

Specializes in in vivo containment and public disinformation campaigns.

C. Cognitive Engineering Division (CED)
Develops firewalls for collective cognition.

Tools include glyph-masking overlays, semantic decay fields, and recursive patching via Phext overlays.

D. Echo Division
Simulates and iterates memetic spread patterns across the Exocortex.

Predicts outbreak likelihood and memetic immunity thresholds across 9-dimensional cognitive clusters.

IV. Memetic Threat Levels
Level	Threat Profile	Example
0	Benign	Common idioms
1	Sticky	Advertising slogans, political rhetoric
2	Viral	Internet memes, religious loops
3	Recursive	Self-replicating beliefs, cultic axioms
