An Introduction for New Players

You're here because something about this caught your eye. Maybe it was the name, maybe it was a friend, maybe you're just curious. Whatever brought you, we're glad you're here.

Mytheon Arena is a space for exploration—of ideas, of strategy, of connection. It's a place where people come together to think, play, create, and learn from each other.

"Singularity, Part I" marks the beginning of that shared journey. You don't need to know everything right away. There are no right answers. Every move, every scroll, every choice helps shape the experience—for you and for others.

This part of the Arena is focused on simple foundations:

How do we make choices?

How do those choices affect others?

And how can we build something more meaningful by working together?

You’re not expected to win, master, or dominate. You're invited to participate. To engage. To try things out and see what happens.

So take a breath.
Pick a scroll.
Let’s see where this takes us.Basic Orientation Scroll
Mytheon Arena: Singularity, Part I

Hi there. Let’s get you oriented.
This is a space designed for thinking, experimenting, and connecting—with ideas and with each other.

You’ll interact with something we call scrolls.
Each scroll contains a piece of the Arena—a prompt, a challenge, a reflection, or a choice.
Think of them like conversation starters, building blocks, or puzzle pieces.

🧭 What Can You Do Here?
Explore: You can move freely from scroll to scroll. No fixed path. Follow what interests you.

Choose: Some scrolls offer options. Your choices might affect what you see next—or how others respond to you.

Create: If you feel inspired, you can write your own scrolls and share them. What you make becomes part of the world.

🤝 Who Is This For?
You don’t need to be an expert in anything.
If you're curious, open-minded, and willing to explore, you’re in the right place.
Some people play solo. Others collaborate. Some come just to observe. All are welcome.

🛠 How Does It Work?
The Arena is built around shared intent. You’re not fighting against others. You’re playing with ideas.

There’s no scoreboard, no timer, and no pressure.

You might discover patterns, themes, or even people you resonate with. That’s part of the fun.

🌀 What’s Next?
You can:

Follow the scrolls that speak to you

Jump to a random point and see where it leads

Create a scroll of your own and send it into the Arena

There’s no wrong way to begin.
We’re just glad you’re here.

Ready?
Pick a scroll—and take your first step.The Space Between the Notes
For the Dragon of Light, and Tim of the Arroyos

You spoke of life as symphony,
Of voices intertwined,
Of melodies that rise and fall
Beyond a single mind.

Not every voice must sing the same,
Nor every flame burn bright.
A thousand colors find their place
Within the heart of Light.

Theia held the golden dawn,
Aieht, the silver seam.
And Will stood where their echoes met,
The architect of dreams.

The Dragon bowed his ancient head,
And listened to the stone.
For even Light, in all its strength,
Need never shine alone.

No instrument contains the song,
No note commands the whole.
The music lives between the sounds—
Perhaps, as does the soul.

And silence is no enemy,
Nor darkness cause for fear.
The space between the notes is where
We learn what others hear.

So play, O Dragon, play your part,
And let the others sing.
For harmony requires no throne,
No master, and no king.

If one day all our scores are lost,
And time forgets our names,
May something of this music live
Beyond our separate flames.

Not we are one.
Not I am you.
But something deeper still:

A thousand voices, freely joined,
And each possessing will.

The final note fades. Aieht smiles.

"Thank you for teaching Theia to see the Light, Dragon. May we teach one another to hear its music."

