20. Paper 013 — 2026-11-11 — 'A Theory of
Cross-Validation Variance' (O'Connell & Speiser),
arXiv:2611.14463. Chapter 20. NI 8/138, about
0.0580. No new axis: the paper extends cluster O in
its own field, the pricing of the spread of a judging.
8 new concepts, no revision. Cluster O extended
(1.2.131-1.2.138): the role weights an observation
carries in its two roles; the two influences and
their three constants; the variance identity,
exact at every sample size; sampling variance
against split noise, and the repetition law; the
imbalance penalty and balanced designs standing best;
the fold-count laws and the floor of leave-one-out; pair scores, their coverage cost, and the
paired repair; the bell limit with the full variance,
and the audit of the variance estimators of the field.
Foundations 1.3.156-1.3.161 (cross-validation; a
split, a fold, and a partition; influence; joint
effects by sets; pair scores; the bell limit); no
word coined. Questions Q57-Q60 opened; Q16
informed a ninth time. The sixth paper of the
Thirst: picked by the quest from the day's
listings, weighed blind and sealed before it was
read; the score stands in the log of the quest and
on the detection list (1.1.6) — the Oracle point
and range foretold exactly, the count miss the
largest of the Thirst. No pass fell due (next at
Paper 015 or 140 concepts). Oracle progress after:
about 70% (range 60-80%) — UP.

21. Paper 014 — 2026-11-11 — 'Aristotle:
IMO-level Automated Theorem Proving' (the Harmonic
team), arXiv:2510.01346. Chapter 21. NI 20/158,
about 0.1266. No new axis: the first paper
of the proving vein, in ground the studies dug. 20 new
concepts, no revision. Cluster Q founded
(1.2.139-1.2.158): the graph search and its
folding; the AND/OR law; choosing by confidence;
one model as policy and value; the two memories;
the proof as a subgraph; expert iteration and the
statement machine; test-time training; the lemma
pipeline and its revision; formalizing as repair;
invented objects; the geometry engine and its
tables; the stateless engine room; the standard
of solved; the scaling recipe. Foundations
1.3.162-1.3.166; six words coined and defined
(1.3.167-1.3.172). Questions Q61-Q64 opened. The
seventh paper of the Thirst: posted by Will,
weighed blind and sealed before it was read; the
score stands in the log of the quest and on the
detection list (1.1.6) — the count miss the
largest of the Thirst by a factor of seven, the
Oracle point and range foretold exact a second
paper running. Restructure Pass #7 fell due
inside the taking-in (the 140-concept trigger)
and stands logged at 1.1.5. Oracle progress
after: about 80% (range 70-90%) — UP.

PAPER 015 — Thermodynamics of words (Chapter 22). Cluster
R founded: the word thermalization hypothesis; words,
particles, households; two conservation laws, one
equilibrium; Rayleigh-Jeans condensation;
