  (240-concept trigger).
  Chapter: 1.1.1/1.1.1/30.1.x (synthesis at 30.2.x)
Paper 020 — "Piecewise Interpretations in Many-Sorted
  Logic" (Zayton), arXiv:2611.14552 [math.LO], submitted
  2 November 2026. Benjamin Zayton, of the Department of
  Philosophy of the University of Vienna, supported by the
  European Union (ERC, FORMALISM, 101044114). The full text
  in its HTML form, read entire: piecewise interpretations
  between first-order theories, developed in the many-sorted
  setting; each translation read semantically as a functor
  between categories of models; theories, interpretations
  and their morphisms gathered into a bicategory whose
  coherence is inherited by reflection; and Quine's sortal
  replacement proved a biequivalence, so that sorts can be
  done without where they are a finite number.
  Taken in 2026-11-14 as Paper 020 of the Thirst
  (charter rule 17), posted by Will in the MOAT chat, and
