5. THE COUNT THAT COUNTS FREELY (Paper 017,
2026-11-13). A silent abstract hides mass (number 1);
a counting abstract can still hide grain. This one's
numbers price the campaign in full — millions of lines
of proof, tens of thousands trusted — and say nothing
about how many concepts the machinery splits into,
because a count of lines is not a count of joints.
The skim priced the frame and the protocols and
missed the joints between them: the tests of the specification, its amendment gate, the grading gate, the
bridge to bytes and its excuse, the priced form of
the reductions, the twice-loaded key. Count the joints, not the weight: where a framework is one machine, its
concepts are its moving parts, and moving parts are
counted by taking the machine apart, not by weighing
it.

At ten scored papers (2026-11-13) the rolling mean of
the misses stands at 0.0166 — the two large misses
(0.0749 and 0.0256) both grain-misses on systems
papers, one silent and one counting — and the axis
calls stand ten for ten, the tenth being the first
no-axis call, landed like the nine axis calls before
it.
Home — state.phext: the ranch, distilled
kind: observed | origin: Muse (this agent) | maintained by: the state-phext-sampler cron (every 5 minutes) running ~/workspace/custom-skills/ranch-state-distillation/scripts/state_sampler.py
source of truth: this file. Raw pulls are working state only, kept outside the phext at ~/workspace/state-sampler/hidden_files/ — never inscribed here.

What this is: every 5 minutes the sampler probes the ranch fleet (17 nodes) through the ranch proxy, writes a one-or-two-line plain-language summary of the cluster (nodes up and down, what is running where, average CPU Tctl, the hotspot), computes the summary's holographic coordinate by Will's Singular method, and stores ONLY the distilled summary as a scroll at that coordinate. No raw telemetry lives in this phext; it stays small and reviewable long-term.

Layout: this Home scroll sits at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1. Every other scroll is one distilled state of the ranch. Its coordinate is the holographic merge of the summary's words — Singular tokenization (letters only; digits carry no words), the component-wise average of each distinct word's atlas position, rounded half up and never below 1, exactly the task-coordinate method — computed over the summary text WITHOUT its timestamp, so a state that reads the same distills to the same coordinate whenever it recurs.

Entry format: one line per pull — "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM TZ | summary". When a new summary computes to a coordinate already occupied, its line is appended inside that scroll with its own timestamp; scrolls are never overwritten and lines are never dropped. Numbers (temperatures, counts) ride inside the line text; the coordinate merges words only, so states differing only in a degree or a count share a scroll, while a changed hotspot or a changed busy set moves the coordinate. If a state ever computed to the Home coordinate itself, it would be stored one scroll past it, at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.2, with its true coordinate noted in the line — the meta line is reserved.

Reading it: scrolls cluster by resemblance — near-identical states sit at near-identical coordinates, so the phext reads as a map of the shapes the ranch takes over time.
Home — lessons.phext: the lessons Will Bickford has taught Emise, each at its own coordinate
kind: observed | origin: Muse (this agent) | built by: ~/workspace/phext/build_lessons_phext.py
source of truth: ~/workspace/phext/lessons-source.phext (sha256 ba8513b01eeb35041fd871a8503919575ef2d20831b7d4c3bb500df1ccccec60) — regenerate
the phext by re-running the builder; never hand-edit this file. Nothing here is published
by the builder; lessons.phext stays local, alongside skills.phext.

What this is: a standalone curation of every lesson Will has given Emise — standing
orders, rulings, and corrections. The 69 lesson scrolls are copied faithfully from
the build for PR #12 (wbic16/human, branch emise/lessons-into-incipit, commit
74c2064ad776107918815d6033e144f921bbc385, 2026-11-06), where the same lessons were added to Incipit.phext.
Curation copies; it does not re-derive or re-word. Each lesson scroll holds the
statement as its first line, the lesson in full, its provenance (date given, source,
[verbatim] or [distilled]), and its derivation note.

Placement: Home alone is assigned, at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1. Every lesson coordinate was
found, not assigned — computed from the lesson statement's exact words by the
Singular holographic merge (task_coordinate.py over the Singular atlas): tokenize
the statement as the Singular checker does; take each distinct word's holographic
position (the average of every CYOA scroll holding the word; a word in Will's
archive but not CYOA rests at home 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1; a word in neither rests at
the far corner 9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.9); average component-wise across the distinct
words, round half up, never below 1. Coordinates are internal to this phext.

Counts: 69 lessons — 6 [verbatim], 63 [distilled].

